  "$comment": "Known-answer vectors for every Σ construction LLO ships (ADR-0047 §5, (DET); bead ley-line-open-10d71a). Each case pins its inputs and, where the construction hashes an encoding, the exact preimage bytes, so a second implementation checks its framing and its hash independently. deriveKey pins the keyed primitive every keyed construction is built on, BLAKE3 derive_key(context, input), with cases taken from BLAKE3's own test_vectors.json (input byte i is i mod 251, first 32 output bytes); it is a primitive, not a construction, and no address in this file moves. Consumed by Rust tests in leyline-core (sigmaBytes, deriveKey, partition, headDigest), leyline-cas-ffi (deriveKey, through the C ABI), leyline-cli-lib (parserId, storeRoot, astNode), the Go module clients/go/leyline-schema (partition, storeRoot, headDigest, astNode; package sigma) and leyline-cache (restrictionKey); run_id is pinned by ../../execution/v1/test-vectors/run-id.json. A changed value is an identity migration that needs a version bump, never an edit.",
